The image shows a single strip of what looks like cooked bacon on a square white plate. The plate is probably about 26 cm across, and the strip is about 18 cm long (roughly 130 px of a 300 px plate width is wrong; the strip spans about 300 px against a plate of about 330 px). That gives a strip of about 20 cm, but it is likely closer to 18 cm, and it is about 1.5 cm wide.

A bacon strip that long and thin is probably a thick-cut or long slice, so I estimate about 12 g cooked. Cooked bacon runs about 5 kcal per gram, which gives roughly 60 kcal. A strip this large could be a bit heavier, so I'll say 15 g and 75 kcal.

